<title>USA: Cold, snow hits central U.S. and more on the way.</title>
<headline>Cold, snow hits central U.S. and more on the way.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snow and cold blanketed much of the central United States early Wednesday and a second blast of cold forecast for Thursday and Friday could damage winter wheat in Kansas and Nebraska, said weather and crop sources .</p>
<p>&quot;All of this is related to a late-season Arctic high pressure system currently centered over the Red River Valley,' said Joel Burgio, meteorologist with Weather Services Corp.</p>
</text>
